The rule: a background cell (0 in test, 4 in demo) becomes 2 when flanked by the pattern color (1/5) on both sides horizontally (and vertically, to be safe).

```python
def transform(grid):
    g = [row[:] for row in grid]
    vals = set(c for row in grid for c in row)
    bg = 0 if 0 in vals else min(vals)
    fg = max(vals)
    H, W = len(g), len(g[0])
    for i in range(H):
        for j in range(W):
            if g[i][j] == bg:
                if j > 0 and j < W-1 and g[i][j-1] == fg and g[i][j+1] == fg:
                    g[i][j] = 2
                elif i > 0 and i < H-1 and g[i-1][j] == fg and g[i+1][j] == fg:
                    g[i][j] = 2
    return g
```

