Demo 2 clarifies: a background cell becomes 2 if there is a pattern-colored cell somewhere to its left AND somewhere to its right in the same row (not just immediate neighbors).

```python
def transform(grid):
    g = [row[:] for row in grid]
    vals = set(c for row in grid for c in row)
    bg = 0 if 0 in vals else min(vals)
    fg = max(vals)
    H, W = len(g), len(g[0])
    for i in range(H):
        fg_cols = [j for j in range(W) if g[i][j] == fg]
        if not fg_cols:
            continue
        lo, hi = min(fg_cols), max(fg_cols)
        for j in range(lo + 1, hi):
            if g[i][j] == bg:
                g[i][j] = 2
    return g
```

